From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
Date: Wed, 25 Mar 2026 15:09:40 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] rz/common/bl2: parse OP-TEE header for BL32 entry width

The RZ BL2 platform setup did not propagate the AArch64 runtime width
flag for the BL32 entry point. Without this, OPTEED initialises the
OP-TEE world with a stale args.arg0 and OP-TEE 4.x boots in the wrong
mode. Set MODE_RW_64 explicitly under SPD_opteed before copying the
entry-point info into bl32_ep_info.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board-specific boot chain integration]

Signed-off-by: Umair Ahmed Shah <umairahmedshah@hotmail.com>
---
 plat/renesas/rz/common/bl2_plat_setup.c | 7 +++++++
 1 file changed, 7 insertions(+)

--- a/plat/renesas/rz/common/bl2_plat_setup.c	2026-03-25 15:09:40.342972215 +0100
+++ b/plat/renesas/rz/common/bl2_plat_setup.c	2026-03-25 15:09:40.345972212 +0100
@@ -53,6 +53,13 @@
 
 	switch (image_id) {
 	case BL32_IMAGE_ID:
+#ifdef SPD_opteed
+		/*
+		 * RZ BL2 does not parse OP-TEE headers. Ensure OPTEED gets
+		 * BL32 runtime width for OP-TEE built as AArch64.
+		 */
+		bl_mem_params->ep_info.args.arg0 = MODE_RW_64;
+#endif
 		memcpy(&params->bl32_ep_info, &bl_mem_params->ep_info,
 			sizeof(entry_point_info_t));
 		break;
